    {
      "id": "KA-C110-tree-on-under",
      "sequence": 4492,
      "title": "ಮರದ ಮೇಲೆ / ಮರದ ಕೆಳಗೆ — on or under the tree",
      "headword": "ಮರದ ಮೇಲೆ ಹಕ್ಕಿ ಇದೆ.",
      "romanization": "marada mēle hakki ide",
      "gloss": "The bird is on the tree — a named reference place",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:c2a3325aec47fdc7",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Guided Practice: on or under",
          "Writing: the place phrases"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: you can do this one in the car, but part of it needs your hands. You can listen to everything else now. I will say so again when we reach them, but leave these sections until you have stopped: Guided Practice: on or under and Writing: the place phrases."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Recall ಮರ (mara, tree) and ಹಕ್ಕಿ (hakki, bird). Point up for ಮೇಲೆ (mēle, on top), then down for ಕೆಳಗೆ (keḷage, under). You know all four words already."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: on the tree",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Listen once. Follow the printed line with your finger:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರದ ಮೇಲೆ ಹಕ್ಕಿ ಇದೆ. marada mēle hakki ide. — The bird is on the tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರದ (marada) means “of the tree” here. It names what ಮೇಲೆ is relative to. Keep ಮರದ ಮೇಲೆ together as “on the tree”; ಹಕ್ಕಿ ಇದೆ says that the bird is there. This one frame does not teach every Kannada noun ending."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar lens: under the tree",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರದ ಕೆಳಗೆ ಹಕ್ಕಿ ಇದೆ. marada keḷage hakki ide. — The bird is under the tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The tree and bird stay the same. Only ಮೇಲೆ changes to ಕೆಳಗೆ. Read both lines aloud, slowly. Listen for the word that tells you where."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice: on or under",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "The bird is on the tree.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: The bird is **on** the tree.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "The bird is under the tree.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: The bird is **under** the tree.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "POINT",
              "instruction": "which printed line puts the bird below?",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU POINT: which printed line puts the bird below?]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: the place phrases",
